STORY=f'''
<section class="page-hero page-hero-story wrap"><div class="page-hero-copy"><div class="micro-label"><span class="micro-dot"></span> THE ORIGIN / 01</div><h1>ONE SUMMER.<br>ONE QUESTION.<br><em>ONE AURA.</em></h1><p>An idea for being more aware outdoors, inspired by a moment close to home.</p><a class="button button-primary" href="#the-moment">Read the story {arrow}</a></div><div class="story-hero-photo"><img src="assets/media/workbench-01.webp" width="1280" height="960" alt="Armaan working on the electronics for Project AURA."><span class="photo-label">ARMAAN JAIN / FOUNDER &amp; INNOVATOR</span><span class="corner-index">01—03</span></div></section>
<div class="chapter-line"><div class="wrap"><span>THE STORY SO FAR</span><span>NEW DELHI, INDIA</span><span>SCROLL TO READ ↓</span></div></div>
<section class="narrative-section section wrap" id="the-moment"><div class="narrative-aside"><span>01</span><small>THE MOMENT<br>THAT STARTED IT</small></div><div class="narrative-main"><div class="section-tag"><span>↗</span> FROM THE FOUNDER’S PITCH <i></i></div><h2>A summer day<br>that <em>stayed with him.</em></h2><p class="large-copy">While playing outside in intense summer heat, Armaan’s older brother fainted. Seeing that moment changed the way Armaan thought about a day in the sun.</p><p>He began asking a simple question: what if people had a better way to notice changing conditions? That question became a starting point for Project AURA.</p><p>AURA is an exploration, not a promise that an incident can be predicted or prevented. Shade, water, rest and appropriate help still matter.</p><a class="text-link" href="research.html">Explore the wider context {arrow}</a></div></section>
<section class="story-quote"><div class="wrap quote-layout"><span class="quote-star" aria-hidden="true">✳</span><blockquote>“Because nobody should have to choose between enjoying the outdoors and staying safe.”</blockquote><div class="quote-credit"><span>ARMAAN JAIN</span><small>PROJECT AURA / FOUNDER’S PITCH</small></div></div></section>
<section class="audience-section section wrap"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="section-tag"><span>02</span> THE VISION <i></i></div><h2>Built from empathy.<br><em>Made for curiosity.</em></h2></div><p>The pitch imagines a future where useful prompts can be easier to understand for people who spend time outdoors.</p></div><div class="audience-grid"><article><span>01 / PLAY</span><h3>Young athletes</h3><p>For people who love sport, play and being outside.</p></article><article><span>02 / EVERY DAY</span><h3>Older adults</h3><p>For people looking for more context in their daily routines.</p></article><article><span>03 / SUN</span><h3>Sensitive skin</h3><p>For those interested in more personalised UV awareness.</p></article></div><p class="tiny-disclaimer">These are intended audiences in the project vision, not a claim that the prototype is safe or effective for any group.</p></section>
<section class="cost-section section"><div class="wrap cost-layout"><div class="cost-intro"><div class="section-tag"><span>03</span> THE ACCESSIBILITY GOAL <i></i></div><h2>Good ideas should<br><em>go further.</em></h2><p>Armaan’s pitch also imagines a more accessible future for wearable awareness.</p></div><div class="cost-pair"><div><span>APPROXIMATE PROTOTYPE BUILD COST</span><strong><small>$</small>40</strong><p>US dollars, as stated in the project pitch.</p></div><div><span>FUTURE PRODUCT TARGET</span><strong><small>$</small>60</strong><p>US dollars, an aspiration for a developed product.</p></div></div><p class="cost-note">These figures are estimates and a future goal, not a current sale price or offer. The prototype is still being developed.</p></div></section>
<section class="founder-section section wrap"><div class="founder-logo"><img src="assets/supercharged-logo.webp" width="1000" height="802" loading="lazy" alt="SUPERCHARGED logo, since 2026"><span>TEAM SUPERCHARGED / 2875</span></div><div class="founder-copy"><div class="section-tag"><span>04</span> THE PERSON BEHIND IT <i></i></div><h2>Hi, I’m Armaan.<br><em>Let’s build.</em></h2><p><strong>Armaan Jain</strong> is the founder and innovator behind AURA and SUPERCHARGED, Team 2875, from The British School, New Delhi.</p><p>The project is part of a journey into robotics, hands-on problem-solving and the Fibonacci International Robot Olympiad. Inspired by UN Sustainable Development Goal 3: Good Health and Well-Being.</p><small>Independent student project; no UN endorsement is implied.</small><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-primary" href="journey.html">See the build {arrow}</a><a class="button button-ghost" href="contact.html">Get in touch {diag}</a></div></div></section>'''

DEVICE=f'''
<section class="page-hero device-hero wrap"><div class="page-hero-copy"><div class="micro-label"><span class="micro-dot"></span> THE WEARABLE / 02</div><h1>SMALL DEVICE.<br><em>BIG QUESTION.</em></h1><p>A closer look at the sensors, screens and experiments inside Project AURA.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-primary" href="#the-system">Explore the system {arrow}</a><a class="button button-ghost" href="#demo">Try the phone app {diag}</a></div><span class="device-hero-note">EXPERIMENTAL PROTOTYPE · NOT A MEDICAL DEVICE</span></div><div class="device-hero-image"><img src="assets/media/prototype-closeup.webp" width="960" height="1280" alt="Photograph of the orange AURA prototype and its display."><div><span>THE REAL PROTOTYPE</span><small>Photo supplied by the project. Values shown are not live.</small></div></div></section>
<div class="chapter-line"><div class="wrap"><span>FOUR SIGNALS</span><span>ONE WRIST-SIZED IDEA</span><span>STILL IN DEVELOPMENT ↗</span></div></div>
<section class="section wrap system-section" id="the-system"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="section-tag"><span>01</span> WHAT’S INSIDE <i></i></div><h2>Different inputs.<br><em>One overview.</em></h2></div><p>Built to experiment with how environmental and vital indicators could be presented together.</p></div><div class="system-grid"><article class="system-card"><div><span>01</span><b>☼</b></div><h3>UV &amp; exposure</h3><p>Estimates UV and tracks approximate exposure time. The sensor mapping is provisional and needs calibration against a reference.</p><small>UV SENSOR / DEMO MAPPING</small></article><article class="system-card"><div><span>02</span><b>〰</b></div><h3>Heart rate</h3><p>An experimental MAX30102 optical signal is used to estimate heart rate when the firmware detects a usable signal.</p><small>OPTICAL / EXPERIMENTAL</small></article><article class="system-card"><div><span>03</span><b>◌</b></div><h3>Blood oxygen</h3><p>The MAX30102 also estimates SpO₂. The current calculation has an 86% floor, which can hide lower calculated values.</p><small>SpO₂ / EXPERIMENTAL</small></article><article class="system-card"><div><span>04</span><b>°</b></div><h3>Temperature</h3><p>A DS18B20 sensor can display values in °C and °F. This is sensor/skin temperature, not a core body temperature.</p><small>DS18B20 / SENSOR READING</small></article></div><div class="prototype-warning"><strong>IMPORTANT PROTOTYPE LIMITS</strong><p>Readings may be inaccurate. The current wrist build places the optical sensor about 1.5 mm from the skin, as reported by the creator; a usable or accurate reading is not guaranteed. The score and alerts are experimental rules, not a diagnosis, medical advice or a validated UV-risk model. Do not rely on AURA for health or safety decisions.</p></div></section>
<section class="section score-section wrap" id="the-score" aria-labelledby="score-title"><div class="score-copy"><div class="section-tag"><span>02</span> THE COMPOSITE SCORE <i></i></div><h2 id="score-title">Different signals.<br><em>One overview.</em></h2><p class="large-copy">An illustrative rule set starts at 100 and subtracts points when its example conditions are met.</p><p>UV, sunscreen timing, heart rate, SpO₂ and sensor temperature all play a part. Choose a scenario to see how the demo changes.</p><details class="score-details"><summary>What goes into the score? <span>+</span></summary><p>UV, sunscreen timing and readings outside selected thresholds can add penalties. Skin type and sensitivity adjust an illustrative UV penalty. Scores 80–100 are labelled Optimal, 55–79 Caution, and below 55 High Risk by these rules. Missing valid heart-rate, SpO₂ or temperature values show <strong>No Data</strong>.</p><p>This is a demo rule set, not a diagnosis or medical advice. The current firmware contains the complete formula.</p></details><div class="score-note"><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#icon-spark"/></svg><span>All values in this interactive panel are simulated examples.</span></div></div><div class="score-workbench" aria-label="Interactive composite score examples"><div class="workbench-head"><span><span class="live-dot"></span> THE SCORE, EXPLAINED</span><span>SIMULATION ONLY</span></div><div class="workbench-main"><div class="score-ring" id="score-ring" role="progressbar" aria-label="Example composite score" aria-valuemin="0" aria-valuemax="100" aria-valuenow="98" style="--score: 98"><div class="score-ring-inner"><small>DEMO SCORE</small><output id="score-value">98</output><span>OUT OF 100</span></div></div><div class="score-state" aria-live="polite"><span class="mini-label">THE READOUT</span><h3 id="scenario-label">Fewer demo flags.</h3><p id="scenario-description">Fewer penalties under these example settings.</p><span class="scenario-badge" id="scenario-band">OPTIMAL · DEMO</span></div></div><div class="examples-heading"><span>CHOOSE AN EXAMPLE</span><span>TYPE NOT SURE · STANDARD</span></div><div class="scenario-buttons" aria-label="Choose a simulated example"><button type="button" data-scenario="baseline" class="is-active" aria-pressed="true">Baseline</button><button type="button" data-scenario="caution" aria-pressed="false">Caution</button><button type="button" data-scenario="high" aria-pressed="false">Multiple signals</button></div><div class="example-values"><div><span>UV INDEX</span><strong id="example-uv">2</strong></div><div><span>HEART RATE</span><strong id="example-hr">78 <small>BPM</small></strong></div><div><span>SpO₂</span><strong id="example-spo2">98<small>%</small></strong></div><div><span>SENSOR TEMP.</span><strong id="example-temp">36.8<small>°C</small></strong></div></div><div class="workbench-foot"><span id="example-spf">SUNSCREEN: LOGGED</span><span>ILLUSTRATIVE RULES, NOT A DIAGNOSIS</span></div></div></section>
<section class="section demo-section" id="demo" aria-labelledby="demo-title"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-heading demo-heading"><div><div class="section-tag"><span>03</span> THE PHONE COMPANION <i></i></div><h2 id="demo-title">Don’t just imagine it.<br><em>Try it.</em></h2></div><p>Explore the actual phone-interface design with simulated examples — no wearable required.</p></div><div class="demo-showcase"><div class="demo-screen"><div class="screen-bar"><span><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><b>PROJECT AURA / PHONE WEB APP</b><span>● SIMULATION</span></div><div class="phone-frame"><iframe src="demo/phone.html" title="AURA phone web app in simulation mode" loading="lazy" sandbox="allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-forms"></iframe></div></div><div class="demo-info"><div class="demo-kicker"><span class="live-dot"></span> INTERACTIVE EXPERIENCE</div><h3>Your AURA,<br> on your phone.</h3><p>Tap through Today, Sun &amp; skin, Alerts and Settings. The preview uses example values, not live readings.</p><a class="button button-primary" href="demo/phone.html">Open the phone app {diag}</a><details class="connection-help"><summary>Have the wearable?</summary><p>Turn on AURA, join Wi-Fi <strong>Project-AURA</strong> (password <strong>12345678</strong>), then open <strong>http://192.168.4.1/</strong> in your phone browser. The device uses demo credentials and unauthenticated HTTP controls; use it only in a trusted space.</p></details><div class="demo-small">SIMULATED EXAMPLES &nbsp; / &nbsp; NO DEVICE REQUIRED</div></div></div><div class="kit-row"><div><span>THE CURRENT DEVICE UPDATE</span><p>The display-only sketch and its matching phone page.</p></div><a class="button button-ghost" href="downloads/project-aura-display-only-update.zip" download>Download the update {arrow}</a></div><div class="kit-row guide-kit-row"><div><span>THE PROJECT GUIDE · 5 PAGE PDF</span><p>A guide to the screens, touch controls and phone companion.</p></div><a class="button button-ghost" href="downloads/project-aura-guide.pdf" download>Download the guide {arrow}</a></div><p class="demo-disclaimer">The hosted app above defaults to simulation. To connect over Wi-Fi, open the page served by the wearable itself. Supported desktop browsers can also use USB Web Serial in a secure context.</p></div></section>
<section class="section screen-section" id="watch-screens"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="section-tag"><span>04</span> ON THE WRIST <i></i></div><h2>Nine screens.<br><em>One little device.</em></h2></div><p>Swipe through the current screen names. These are illustrations, not readings from a connected watch.</p></div><div class="screen-toolbar"><span>SCREEN INDEX / SWIPE TO EXPLORE →</span><div><button type="button" data-screen-nav="-1" aria-label="Scroll screens left" aria-controls="screen-rail">←</button><button type="button" data-screen-nav="1" aria-label="Scroll screens right" aria-controls="screen-rail">→</button></div></div><div class="screen-rail" id="screen-rail" tabindex="0" aria-label="Nine watch screen illustrations; scroll horizontally"><article><div class="oled-screen"><small>AURA / 01</small><strong>HOME</strong><em>score overview</em></div><h3>Home &amp; score</h3></article><article><div class="oled-screen"><small>AURA / 02</small><strong>♥</strong><em>heart rate</em></div><h3>Heart rate</h3></article><article><div class="oled-screen"><small>AURA / 03</small><strong>SpO₂</strong><em>oxygen estimate</em></div><h3>Blood oxygen</h3></article><article><div class="oled-screen"><small>AURA / 04</small><strong>°C / °F</strong><em>sensor temperature</em></div><h3>Temperature</h3></article><article><div class="oled-screen"><small>AURA / 05</small><strong>☼ UV</strong><em>sun + sunscreen</em></div><h3>UV &amp; SPF</h3></article><article><div class="oled-screen"><small>AURA / 06</small><strong>▰</strong><em>power + link</em></div><h3>Battery &amp; link</h3></article><article><div class="oled-screen"><small>AURA / 07</small><strong>!</strong><em>alert overview</em></div><h3>Alerts</h3></article><article><div class="oled-screen"><small>AURA / 08</small><strong>◷</strong><em>clock</em></div><h3>Clock</h3></article><article><div class="oled-screen"><small>AURA / 09</small><strong>AQI</strong><em>coming soon</em></div><h3>AQI · coming soon</h3></article></div><p class="tiny-disclaimer">The battery percentage is a voltage-based estimate. AQI is a placeholder, not a measurement.</p></div></section>
<section class="section wrap gesture-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="section-tag"><span>05</span> A LITTLE MORE DETAIL <i></i></div><h2>Made to be<br><em>explored.</em></h2></div><p>One touch control, experimental reminders and a growing list of ideas.</p></div><div class="gesture-grid"><article><strong>01</strong><h3>One tap</h3><p>Advance the display or acknowledge an alert.</p></article><article><strong>02</strong><h3>Double tap</h3><p>Switch between Standard and Sensitive modes.</p></article><article><strong>03</strong><h3>Hold ~1 second</h3><p>Log sunscreen in the prototype’s timer.</p></article><article class="coming-card"><strong>+</strong><h3>AQI <span>COMING SOON</span></h3><p>A future placeholder — there is no AQI measurement in this prototype.</p></article></div><div class="device-faq"><details><summary>How do the skin and sensitivity settings work? <span>+</span></summary><p>The app supports a self-reported skin type and a separate Standard or Sensitive setting. These adjust illustrative UV rules; they are not validated personalised protection advice or safe-exposure limits.</p></details><details><summary>When can I see an alert on the phone? <span>+</span></summary><p>The watch runs its experimental alert rules locally. Phone alerts depend on the app page being open and connected. Readings and prompts should not be relied on for health or safety decisions.</p></details><details><summary>How should I charge the prototype? <span>+</span></summary><p>Remove the device, switch the battery OFF and unplug ESP32 USB before charging. Unplug the charger before switching the battery ON. Do not charge unattended; stop if the battery becomes hot, swollen or damaged.</p></details></div></section>'''

